  "neosmartuiLearningSignals": [
    "The public Figma preview directly verifies 39 distinct UI component families (15 utility + 24 interactive). This is the semantic breadth benchmark; the 5k+ smart-components claim is not used as a distinct-component count.",
    "Riddle UI is a strong design-system breadth benchmark rather than a code-registry benchmark.",
    "Its separation of foundations, utility elements, interactive components, pages and marketing sections reinforces NeoSmartUI's own layered architecture.",
    "Advanced patterns visible in the Figma preview—coach marks, datepicker, file uploader, steps, tables, charts, notifications, stacked lists and action panels—are useful gap-analysis inputs for the 90+ Core expansion.",
    "The 160+ example-sections claim is more relevant to future Blocks/Pages breadth than to Core component counting.",
    "Framer + Figma dual delivery is a useful benchmark for designer workflows; NeoSmartUI should preserve its stronger code/contract/public-proof architecture rather than copy Riddle's asset model."
  ],
  "planning": {
    "neosmartuiCoreTarget": "90+ distinct public-proof Core components",
    "countsAreBenchmarkOnly": true,
    "countIntegrityNote": "Riddle marketing counts must not be converted directly into NeoSmartUI semantic component counts.",
    "trackedCompetitorComparison": "Riddle's 39 directly verified UI families are below neobrutalism.com's 57 public component documentation routes and neobrutalism.dev's 61 unique UI implementation files. NeoSmartUI's 90+ distinct public-proof Core target remains above every currently verified tracked-competitor semantic/component breadth count."
  }
